# maze-hardening: NetworkManager is Maze's one network manager.
#
# systemd's own preset (90-systemd.preset) enables systemd-networkd and
# systemd-networkd-wait-online. Presets are applied on a system's first boot
# (no /etc/machine-id yet) — which is EVERY boot of the live ISO. The live
# system then ran NetworkManager and systemd-networkd side by side on the same
# interfaces, and systemd-networkd-wait-online held network-online.target (and
# everything ordered after it: entropy-shield, reflector, maze-flatpak-setup,
# ollama) for its full 2-minute timeout whenever networkd had no link of its
# own to bring up — i.e. on Wi-Fi, which NetworkManager handles.
#
# This file sorts before 90-systemd.preset, so its lines win. The installed
# system never re-applies presets on its own (its machine-id is set at install
# time); maze-installer disables these units there explicitly.
disable systemd-networkd.service
disable systemd-networkd.socket
disable systemd-networkd-*.socket
disable systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
disable systemd-networkd-wait-online@.service
disable systemd-networkd-persistent-storage.service
